    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad1edff1_f129bc4c",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 5305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1124150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-07T20:54:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "config.meteredHint changes via ExternalScoreEvaluator, which calls WifiConfigManager#addOrUpdateNetwork. handleSupplicantStateChange will in turn update the capabilities to match when a connection is made. The Settings UI will also call the same method to update config.meteredOverride.\n\nIt is worth noting that this means when user toggles a network as metered within Settings UI, the capability change will only happen on the next connection. That seems acceptable because the UI is not used often, thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "cd47938e_8429079d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5305,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 5305,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "b9f326b3ef1be3bafae2f5cbb89a7831cccc24db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2d3f4f99_6eb36fcb",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 5305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
