      "writtenOn": "2016-12-08T23:49:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, if I\u0027m reading the code correctly, it doesn\u0027t seem hard to have this take effect dynamically.\n\nIf you make the settings UI call WifiManager#updateNetwork, then it will result in WifiStateMachine getting CMD_ADD_OR_UPDATE_NETWORK and calling WifiConfigManager#addOrUpdateNetwork for you, on the right thread.\n\nThen all you need to do is make sure that the handling code for CMD_ADD_OR_UPDATE_NETWORK calls updateCapabilities() if the update succeeded and the network is the current network. Then the metered bit will be updated properly.\n\nRoshan, I assume this is safe to do?",
      "parentUuid": "ad1edff1_f129bc4c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5305,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 5305,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "b9f326b3ef1be3bafae2f5cbb89a7831cccc24db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
